    "Notes Updated": "10/1/2023",
    "Scouting Notes": "Starter?\n Fastball seems to have been pushed into a 2S/CT combo more than the 4S I originally saw. Don't know that I love it, but they both flash decently.\n Sitting more in the lower 90's now, but still touching 95 in a few looks.\n Slider is wicked. Nasty vertical movement and sharp. Up to 87 MPH, mostly in the 82 84 range.\n Still showing what appears to be a pretty decent curve as well, in the 79 82 range.\n Command was a problem this year, though he limited walks to a decent degree. Needs to hit spots better in the zone.",
    "Notes Updated 2": "8/28/2022",
    "Scouting Notes 2": "Starter?\n  Fastball shows really good life at the top of the zone and is up to 97\n  Slider is wicked. Nasty vertical movement and sharp. Up to 87 MPH.\n  Showed a pretty decent curve as well, at least I think it was a curve. Looked slower than his slider, but the vertical movement was similar.\n  Command was decent if not great and he hasn't shown many walk issues so far.\n  Didn't pitch at all at Eastern Michigan his last season (academically ineligible). Brewers might have a major 11th round steal.",
